sh of the Styx the wrathful strike and bite each other. The sullen lie beneath the water, and their sighs rise as bubbles."}, {"titolo": "Guardian", "testo": "Phlegyas, the ferryman who carries Dante across the Styx to the walls of the city of Dis."}], "verso_it": "Fitti nel limo dicon: “Tristi fummo\nne l’aere dolce che dal sol s’allegra,\nportando dentro accidïoso fummo:", "verso_en": "Fixed in the mire they say, ‘We sullen were\nIn the sweet air, which by the sun is gladdened,\nBearing within ourselves the sluggish reek;", "cita": "Inferno VII, 121–123", "gioco": "In the full game, Inferno."}, {"id": "eresia", "colore": "#ff7a2e", "mappa": {"r": 41.7, "a": 6.17}, "stato": "gioco", "kicker": "Circle VI", "nome": "Heresy", "nome_it": "Eretici", "canto": "Inferno IX–XI", "immagine": "", "immagine_alt": "", "sezioni": [{"titolo": "The sin", "testo": "The heretics, who denied that the soul lives on after death, as Epicurus and his followers did."}, {"titolo": "The punishment", "testo": "Inside the walls of the city of Dis they lie in open tombs, burning. The lids will close on Judgement Day."}, {"titolo": "Guardian", "testo": "The Furies and Medusa defend the gate of Dis, until a messenger from Heaven opens it."}], "verso_it": "Vedi là Farinata che s’è dritto:\nda la cintola in sù tutto ’l vedrai.", "verso_en": "Behold there Farinata who has risen;\nFrom the waist upwards wholly shalt thou see him.", "cita": "Inferno X, 32–33", "gioco": "In the full game, Inferno."}, {"id": "violenza", "colore": "#ff3d2b", "mappa": {"r": 33.5, "a": 6.99}, "stato": "gioco", "kicker": "Circle VII", "nome": "Violence", "nome_it": "Violenti", "canto": "Inferno XII–XVII", "immagine": "", "immagine_alt": "", "sezioni": [{"titolo": "The sin", "testo": "The violent, in three rings: against others, against themselves, and against God, nature and art."}, {"titolo": "The punishment", "testo": "Tyrants and murderers boil in the Phlegethon, a river of blood watched by centaurs. Suicides become thorny trees torn by the Harpies. Blasphemers, sodomites and usurers burn on a desert of sand under a slow rain of fire."}, {"titolo": "Guardian", "testo": "The Minotaur."}], "verso_it": "Sovra tutto ’l sabbion, d’un cader lento,\npiovean di foco dilatate falde,\ncome di neve in alpe sanza vento.", "verso_en": "O’er all the sand-waste, with a gradual fall,\nWere raining down dilated flakes of fire,\nAs of the snow on Alp without a wind.", "cita": "Inferno XIV, 28–30", "gioco": "In the full game, Inferno."}, {"id": "frode", "colore": "#ffa04d", "mappa": {"r": 25.7, "a": 7.81}, "stato": "gioco", "kicker": "Circle VIII", "nome": "Fraud", "nome_it": "Fraudolenti · Malebolge", "canto": "Inferno XVIII–XXX", "immagine": "", "immagine_alt": "", "sezioni": [{"titolo": "The sin", "testo": "Fraud against those who had no reason to trust: panderers and seducers, flatterers, simonists, soothsayers, corrupt officials, hypocrites, thieves, false counsellors, sowers of discord and falsifiers."}, {"titolo": "The punishment", "testo": "Ten stone ditches, the Malebolge, each with its own torment: whipped by demons, plunged in boiling pitch, crushed under cloaks of lead, wrapped in flames."}, {"titolo": "Guardian", "testo": "Geryon, the monster of fraud, with the face of an honest man and a scorpion's tail, carries Dante down on his back."}], "verso_it": "Considerate la vostra semenza:\nfatti non foste a viver come bruti,\nma per seguir virtute e canoscenza.", "verso_en": "Consider ye the seed from which ye sprang;\nYe were not made to live like unto brutes,\nBut for pursuit of virtue and of knowledge.", "cita": "Inferno XXVI, 118–120", "gioco": "In the full game, Inferno."}, {"id": "tradimento", "colore": "#9ee8ff", "mappa": {"r": 11.5, "a": 8.63}, "stato": "gioco", "kicker": "Circle IX", "nome": "Treachery", "nome_it": "Traditori · Cocito", "canto": "Inferno XXXI–XXXIV", "immagine": "", "immagine_alt": "", "sezioni": [{"titolo": "The sin", "testo": "Treachery, the gravest fraud, against